  "title": "LLMNR: Request response tracking",
  "description": "LLMNR (over UDP - we don't dissect it over TCP, and Microsoft indicates\nthat they don't necessarily support it over TCP) sends queries to\nlink-scope multicast addresses, and responses \"MUST be sent to the sender\nvia unicast.\" (https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4795#section-2.2\nhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc4795#section-2.3)\n\nSo ordinary conversation tracking doesn't work here - the conversation\nshould match only the address of the original sender.\n\nmDNS also has multicast handling, but is different - there the responses\nare sent on multicast, but also the query ID field isn't used and is\nalmost always 0, and the questions are not repeated in the response message,\nso request-response tracking is very difficult and probably shouldn't\nbe done at all.\n\nFix #20723\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 32d5f139a94e6bf7af6ff55a9b29613758d3cdb9)\n\nCo-authored-by: John Thacker <johnthacker@gmail.com>",
